(2831029, 391432, 33515, '<td valign="top">Diego I am very surprised at this finish, this is a much better photograph than 5.7. Anyone who questions this being rule of thirds needs to read a book. So very well done. The best thing about this photo is that it is natural, no set up, no lighting, no high priced models, just a shot you saw and photographed.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-13 09:45:30.</i></td>', 'Diego I am very surprised at this finish, this is a much better photograph than 5.7. Anyone who questions this being rule of thirds needs to read a book. So very well done. The best thing about this photo is that it is natural, no set up, no lighting, no high priced models, just a shot you saw and photographed.', '2006-09-13 10:39:45.000000', '2006-09-13 10:45:30.000000', 0),
(2831032, 391522, 28710, '<td valign="top">at 30th place, I''d call this underrated. very strong composition and coloring...<br/> <br/>probably lost a bit due to the oddly strong grain and visible color gradients...<br/> <br/>Could stand to be just a hair sharper too...<br/> <br/>Otherwise a fantastic image that is almost emotive.</td>', 'at 30th place, I''d call this underrated. very strong composition and coloring... probably lost a bit due to the oddly strong grain and visible color gradients... Could stand to be just a hair sharper too... Otherwise a fantastic image that is almost emotive.', '2006-09-13 10:40:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2831052, 391187, 28710, '<td valign="top">Nice use of color contrasts. Colors seem a bit uncomfortable though...<br/> <br/>The border doesn''t seem to be quite right. I would have gone with a softer border, maybe with pinks and whites or reds or something...<br/> <br/>Aside from that, it seems like there is nice depth.<br/> <br/>An interesting aside, there is an expression in Chinese here in Taiwan called ''cao mei'' meaning strawberry. It indicates that a person has a very thin skin and is ill suited to hard work or oppression of any sort.<br/> <br/>It is in reference to the recent (last 30 years or so) upswing in the economy here which has led to a lot of very hard working parents with not very hard working children... such that they study so much they don''t go outside and don''t even like to walk or go out in the sun away from the a/c.<br/> <br/>The older generation looks down on them and calls them a bunch of strawberries.<br/> <br/>The expression is sometimes explained by referencing the difference between a strawberry and an apple (as it was in class yesterday).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-13 09:47:02.</i></td>', 'Nice use of color contrasts. Colors seem a bit uncomfortable though... The border doesn''t seem to be quite right. I would have gone with a softer border, maybe with pinks and whites or reds or something... Aside from that, it seems like there is nice depth. An interesting aside, there is an expression in Chinese here in Taiwan called ''cao mei'' meaning strawberry. It indicates that a person has a very thin skin and is ill suited to hard work or oppression of any sort. It is in reference to the recent (last 30 years or so) upswing in the economy here which has led to a lot of very hard working parents with not very hard working children... such that they study so much they don''t go outside and don''t even like to walk or go out in the sun away from the a/c. The older generation looks down on them and calls them a bunch of strawberries. The expression is sometimes explained by referencing the difference between a strawberry and an apple (as it was in class yesterday).', '2006-09-13 10:46:13.000000', '2006-09-13 10:47:02.000000', 0),
(2831060, 390626, 28710, '<td valign="top">Your pictures always blow my mind... such a broad range of styles...<br/> <br/>Well done on using the water''s refractive qualities...</td>', 'Your pictures always blow my mind... such a broad range of styles... Well done on using the water''s refractive qualities...', '2006-09-13 10:49:06.000000', NULL, 0),
