(2864368, 389949, 48389, '<td valign="top">OK here goes, for the most part I am ignoring the challenge title....<br/> <br/>The first thing that hits me in this shot is the blown out parts at the top of the frame and the orange glow in the top right hand corner. I would crop those out immediately allowing the viewer to be drawn to the ''grass'' rather than elsewhere. <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=401503" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/48389/thumb/401503.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/48389/thumb/401503.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/48389/thumb/401503.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I love the backlighting but would like to see more detail in the ''head''. The DOF is good as it is blurred enough to not allow any distractions to the main focus.<br/> <br/>In comparison with <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=397127" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/556/thumb/397127.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/556/thumb/397127.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/556/thumb/397127.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Obviously this shot is much closer and therefore there is a lot more detail which I like. For me the blades of grass in the background of this shot are distracting but the green tones are good and I think the crop works fairly well.<br/> <br/>The two shots, although of a similar subject are very different and both have good and bad points. <br/> <br/>Overall I think you have spotted this well and if cropping would have allowed you to stay in the rule of thirds, IMHO this would have helped the shot.</td>', 'OK here goes, for the most part I am ignoring the challenge title.... The first thing that hits me in this shot is the blown out parts at the top of the frame and the orange glow in the top right hand corner. I would crop those out immediately allowing the viewer to be drawn to the ''grass'' rather than elsewhere.    I love the backlighting but would like to see more detail in the ''head''. The DOF is good as it is blurred enough to not allow any distractions to the main focus. In comparison with   Obviously this shot is much closer and therefore there is a lot more detail which I like. For me the blades of grass in the background of this shot are distracting but the green tones are good and I think the crop works fairly well. The two shots, although of a similar subject are very different and both have good and bad points.  Overall I think you have spotted this well and if cropping would have allowed you to stay in the rule of thirds, IMHO this would have helped the shot.', '2006-09-25 20:54:37.000000', NULL, 0),
